cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LLM-LCI: a locate-and-quote assistant for life-cycle inventory assumptions in LCA papers"
abstract: >-
  Research code from the 2026 Duke Kunshan University Summer Research Scholars
  program. Given a question about a life-cycle inventory assumption, it returns
  the study, the section or table that states the assumption, and a verbatim
  quote. Hybrid dense and BM25 retrieval finds candidate papers; a long-context
  LLM reads one paper per call; the section is resolved in Python from the quote.
authors:
  - family-names: Tojiyev
    given-names: Dovudxon
    affiliation: Duke Kunshan University
date-released: "2026-10-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/David33706/LLM-LCI"
keywords:
  - life cycle assessment
  - life cycle inventory
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - large language models
  - information retrieval
  - hybrid search
  - BM25
